61:## API (everything a screen's own code may use; import from the app's `src/kit`)
62:
63:```tsx
64:import { KitScreen, KitWidget, useKit, type KitData } from '../../kit';
65:```
66:
67:- `<KitScreen screen={kit} dialogs={{ d1: DialogD1 }} services={services} shell?>`: already in the ported Page.tsx. `screen` is
68:  the screen's `kit.json`; `dialogs` maps each dialog id to its body component; `services` is `src/services/<screen>.ts`.
69:- `<KitWidget id="k3" />`: one Kendo widget, by the id the capture stamped. Already placed by the port.
70:- `useKit()` (inside a KitScreen, e.g. in a dialog body or a small component of the screen) returns
71:  `{ data, defs, bus, openDialog }`:
72:  - `bus.on('change', ({ name, id, value }) => …)`: a kit widget's value changed (returns an unsubscribe function);
73:    `bus.on('search', (values) => …)` after Search; `bus.on('reset', () => …)` after Reset. `bus.emit(type, detail)` sends one.
74:    Plain inputs (text boxes, radios, checkboxes) are not on the bus: listen to their DOM events.
75:  - `openDialog('d2')`: open a captured dialog from code (e.g. a radio that opens one).
76:  - `data`: the kit.json (`widgets`, `dialogs`, `grids`, `search`, `row`, `plan`, `missing`).
77:- Services (`src/services/<screen>.ts`): `search(values)` returns `{ total, rows }` of synthetic rows; `save(dialog, values)`.
78:  `endpoints` names the live endpoints. Edit freely: it is generated once.
79:- Attributes the kit acts on (keep them): `data-kit-action="search|reset|cancel|create|save|close|collapse|menu|menu-close"`,
80:  `data-kit-tip="text"` (a tooltip), `data-kit-h` (hidden at rest; Search reveals the ones in `search.reveals`),
81:  `data-kit-collapse` (a panel body), `data-kit-menu*` (the side menu: never touch it from a screen).
82:
83:Worked example: the FTP Server Credentials screen needs no code of its own beyond the port. Its Create New opens dialog `d1`
84:("Add FTP Server Credentials", ported to `dialogs/DialogD1.tsx`), its tooltips and validation come from the kit, and its grid
85:fills on Search. A screen with a conditional field adds one small component next to the markup, for example:
86:
87:```tsx
88:// shows the part hidden at rest (data-kit-h="h4") only for "Run Monthly", as the screen's script does
89:function RunSchedule() {
90:  useEffect(() => {
91:    const on = (e: Event) => {
92:      const r = e.target as HTMLInputElement;
93:      if (r.name === 'RunSchedule') document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-kit-h="h4"]')!.style.display = r.value === 'M' ? '' : 'none';
94:    };
95:    document.addEventListener('change', on);
96:    return () => document.removeEventListener('change', on);
97:  }, []);
98:  return null;
99:}
100:```
