102:## The side menu (the shell, built by the kit)
103:
104:Measured on the live portal (docs/provider-probe, probe 2): the hamburger swaps the menu root's classes (`display-none` →
105:`display-flex`, which are `!important`) and appends `<div class="disabled-backdrop">` to `<body>`; there is no fade. A module
106:flies out to the left after Kendo's hover delay (100 ms) with its menu animation (open 200 ms, close 100 ms). Only the X and a
107:menu link close it: Escape and a click on the backdrop do not. The capture records all of this on the menu root
108:(`data-kit-menu-add/-remove/-backdrop/-hover/-open-ms/-close-ms`) and the kit replays it; a link to a rebuilt screen routes there.
109:
110:A module's submenu is a box **beside** the module list, not inside it: Kendo lifts the popup out of the `<ul>` (which clips what
111:is inside) into a `.k-animation-container` on the menu's scroll wrapper, `left: -width; top: <the item's top>` for the vertical
112:side menu, under the item for the horizontal **module tab** (`#activeModuleMenu`, "CLAIMS MANAGEMENT ∨" under the header). The
113:kit does the same for both (`[data-kit-flyout]`), with each menu's own timings (stamped on the `<ul>`). A module the capture
114:itself hovered no longer has its popup inside its `<li>`: Kendo left it in that container, linked by `data-groupparent` (on the
115:item) and `data-group` (on the popup); the kit finds it there (this is the module of the pack, hovered for the fly-out check: the
116:rebuilt menu once opened every module except that one). Only a link to a screen of
117:this app navigates (and closes the menu); every other item is shown and leads nowhere, so the whole menu can be browsed. **Quick
118:Links** (`#mobileMenuIcon`) is a collapsible shell panel: the capture stamps it (`collapse`) and the kit toggles its angle icon,
119:`subpanel-collapsed`, title and body like the portal's `expandPanel`. The **page help book** (`.help-icon-container`) belongs to
120:the page, not the shell: each screen's `screen.json` `help` is its markup or null, and the screen shows or hides it.
121:`kit/states` check all of it on the rebuild (`menu-open`, `menu-flyout`, `tab-flyout`, `menu-close`): the fly-out must be on top and
122:outside the list, and look like the live one. Captures from before this have no `menu-flyout`/`tab-flyout`/`help`: capture again.
