Implemented the missing “screen script” behavior for `fxfer-v6/home` (only what the kit can’t know) by wiring up the hidden-at-rest parts and legacy `javascript:` hooks.

**Changes**
- Added `src/screens/home/HomeBehavior.tsx` to:
  - Toggle responsive hidden blocks (`orientationPortrait` / `orientationLandscape`, `.mobile-nav` at `<1280px`).
  - Provide safe global legacy functions used by the ported markup (`getBroadcastMsg`, `getFavorites`, `getContactUs`, `getAudit`/`getMail`/`getNotes`/`getReports`/`getPrintPreview`/`getReturnToProvider`, `toggleVisibility*`, `popupCenteredWindow`, etc).
  - Implement open/close behavior for:
    - Header accessory panels (External Links / Messages / Favorites / Contact Us) via `visibility` (matches CSS behavior).
    - MCB panels via `display-none` toggling.
    - Footer policy panel open (Disclaimer / Website Requirements / Privacy Policy / Cookie Policy) and close (`button-close-8`).
- Mounted it from `src/screens/home/Page.tsx` without touching `src/kit` or `src/shell`.

**Checks**
- `npx tsc --noEmit` (in `packs/fxfer-v6/app`): PASS
- Visual/behavior verify (had to use IPv4 to avoid `localhost`/IPv6 refusal):
  - `URL=http://127.0.0.1:5180/#/ WAIT_ROOT=1 node scripts/verify.mjs fxfer-v6/home`
  - Result: `states: 7/8 match the live page | ✗ menu-flyout@client: 22.68% off` (the one pre-known failure)

Skipped: removing the existing React whitespace/hydration console warnings in the mechanical port (would require risky large markup edits). Risk: some overlay contents remain whatever the capture already included; no new content was invented.
